<title>USA: DeKalb considering stock dividend.</title>
<headline>DeKalb considering stock dividend.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>DeKalb Genetics Corp said Wednesday it was considering a stock dividend of one share of stock for each outstanding share.</p>
<p>During a meeting with institutional investors, chairman and chief exeuctive Bruce Bickner said the company's management would ask DeKalb's board to approve the stock dividend at a July 10 meeting.  </p>
<p>The stock dividend would be distributed later this summer if the company's board approves it, the company said.</p>
<p>The total number of DeKalb's outstanding class A shares would rise to about 4.8 million from 2.4 million. The number of class B shares would rise to about 29.6 million from 14.8 million.</p>
<p>	    -- Reuter Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
